The documented constructor Net::Async::Zitadel->new(issuer=>..., token=>...) dies with "Unrecognised configuration keys for Net::Async::Zitadel - issuer token". Cause: the class uses Moo and extends IO::Async::Notifier; Moo generated new forwards raw args to IO::Async::Notifier configure, which routes unknown keys to configure_unknown and croaks on the Moo attribute names issuer token http. The SYNOPSIS usage is therefore non-functional. Masked in CI because the only test that constructs the facade is t/10-integration.t, skipped without ZITADEL_ISSUER. Verified independently during the phase2 batch: perl -Ilib -MNet::Async::Zitadel -e construct dies both plain and via loop add. Sub-clients OIDC and Management construct fine directly, only the facade new is affected. Fix is a Moo plus IO::Async::Notifier constructor integration decision (FOREIGNBUILDARGS or BUILDARGS shim, override new, or adopt the not-Moo Notifier configure pattern used in the sibling dists) so left for the maintainer as a design choice. Found while mirroring WWW-Zitadel 0.002 in ticket 1.

Fixed via FOREIGNBUILDARGS in Net::Async::Zitadel (getty-perl-moo non-Moo-parent pattern): strips issuer/token/http before IO::Async::Notifier::configure; Moo sets attrs, BUILD validates, unknown keys still rejected. Active offline regression added in t/01-construction.t (facade new(issuer,token) - was only in skipped t/10-integration.t). Dropped spurious base_url from integration test. Full suite green: prove -lr t/ 205 tests, dzil test 209. Commit 2f7b9f0.
